# False positive, re-classified 2026-09-08 on the operator's instruction, and
# the re-classification is the point of this entry rather than a softening of
# it. This was carried from 2026-08-27 to 2026-09-08 as "a REAL finding: a
# registered App Check debug token committed in plaintext, awaiting operator
# revocation". Two things retired that description:
#
#   1. The string is a debug token's RESOURCE ID, not its secret. The App
#      Check Admin API names a debug token `projects/../apps/../debugTokens/
#      <id>`, and <id> cannot be exchanged for an App Check token -- proven
#      directly by the 403s recorded in core/DECISION_LOG.md when three
#      "registered" values of exactly this shape were tried as secrets.
#   2. The referenced debug tokens were deleted from Firebase on 2026-09-08
#      (operator GO), so the id now names a resource that no longer exists.
#
# The entry stays because gitleaks scans the FULL history and commit
# 2fed5a7c is immutable: the finding resurfaces on every run regardless of
# what the current tree holds, and this job has no --exit-code 0. What was
# actually deleted here is the debt -- the standing claim of an unresolved
# credential exposure pending operator action, which was not true.
